.SH NAME
frontend/node_modules/detect-node-es Directory Reference
.SH SYNOPSIS
.br
.PP
.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 

.SH "detect-node"
.PP
.RS 4
This is a fork of \fRdetect-node\fP\&. 
.RE
.PP

.PP
Differences:
.IP "\(bu" 2
uses named export {isNode}
.IP "\(bu" 2
has d\&.ts integrated
.IP "\(bu" 2
supports ESM
.PP
.SS "Install"
.PP
.nf
npm install \-\-save detect\-node\-es
.fi
.PP
.SS "Usage:"
.PP
.nf
\-var isNode = require('detect\-node');
+var {isNode} = require('detect\-node\-es');

if (isNode) {
  console\&.log("Running under Node\&.JS");
} else {
  alert("Hello from browser (or whatever not\-a\-node env)");
}
.fi
.PP

.PP
The check is performed as: 
.PP
.nf
module\&.exports = false;

// Only Node\&.JS has a process variable that is of [[Class]] process
try {
 module\&.exports = Object\&.prototype\&.toString\&.call(global\&.process) === '[object process]' 
} catch(e) {}

.fi
.PP

.PP
Thanks to Ingvar Stepanyan for the initial idea\&. This check is both \fBthe most reliable I could find\fP and it does not use \fRprocess\fP env directly, which would cause browserify to include it into the build\&. 
